---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { listings, avatar, fmtDate } from '../../lib/data';
import affiliates from '../../data/affiliates.json';
const cw = listings.find(l => l.slug === 'chatwoot--chatwoot')!;
const aff = (affiliates as Record<string, { href: string; label: string; terms: string }>)['chatwoot--chatwoot'];
const CHECKED = 'Oct 23, 2026';
const S = {
  cloud: 'https://www.chatwoot.com/pricing',
  self: 'https://www.chatwoot.com/pricing/self-hosted-plans/',
  req: 'https://developers.chatwoot.com/self-hosted/deployment/requirements',
  do: 'https://www.digitalocean.com/pricing/droplets',
  vultr: 'https://www.vultr.com/pricing/',
};
const cloud = [
  { plan: 'Hacker', price: '$0', note: 'up to 2 agents, 500 conversations/month, live chat only, 30 days of data retention; no help center, automation or AI' },
  { plan: 'Startups', price: '$19 per agent/mo', note: 'unlimited conversations (fair use), help center, 300 Captain AI credits/month; no automation rules or teams' },
  { plan: 'Business', price: '$39 per agent/mo', note: 'adds automation rules, voice, teams, 500 Captain AI credits/month' },
  { plan: 'Enterprise', price: 'Not listed', note: 'adds SSO/SAML, audit logs, 3-year data retention, 800 Captain AI credits/month' },
];
const self = [
  { plan: 'Community Edition', price: '$0', note: 'the open-source app on your own server; help comes from Discord and GitHub' },
  { plan: 'Premium Support', price: '$19 per agent/mo', note: 'custom branding, agent capacity, roles and permissions, priority email support' },
  { plan: 'Enterprise Edition', price: '$99 per agent/mo', note: 'adds Captain AI, voice calls, SSO/SAML, SLA policies, phone support and dev office hours' },
];
const sizes = [2, 3, 5, 10, 20];
const SERVER = 24; // DigitalOcean 2 vCPU / 4 GiB Basic Droplet, read Oct 21, 2026
const maxV = 20 * 39;
const faq = [
  { q: 'How much does Chatwoot cost?', a: 'Chatwoot Cloud is free for up to 2 agents and 500 conversations a month. Paid plans are $19 per agent per month (Startups) and $39 per agent per month (Business); Enterprise has no public price (chatwoot.com/pricing, checked Oct 23, 2026).' },
  { q: 'Is self-hosted Chatwoot free?', a: 'Yes. The Community Edition is $0 per agent. You pay for a server (Chatwoot asks for at least 4 GB RAM) and your own time. Paid self-hosted plans are $19 per agent per month for Premium Support and $99 for Enterprise Edition.' },
  { q: 'When is self-hosting Chatwoot cheaper?', a: 'Almost as soon as you pass the free cloud plan. Two agents on Business is $78 a month; a 4 GB server is about $20–24 a month. The catch is that the free Community Edition leaves out Captain AI, voice and roles, and you run upgrades and backups yourself.' },
];
const schema = [
  { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'Article', headline: 'Chatwoot pricing: cloud plans vs self-hosting', dateModified: '2026-10-23', author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'SelfHost Office' }, mainEntityOfPage: new URL('/pricing/chatwoot/', Astro.site).toString() },
  { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'FAQPage', mainEntity: faq.map(f => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })) },
];
---
<Base title="Chatwoot pricing (Oct 2026): cloud plans vs self-hosting, per-agent cost" description="Chatwoot Cloud is free for 2 agents, then $19 or $39 per agent per month. Self-hosted Community Edition is $0 plus a 4 GB server. Worked monthly costs for 2 to 20 agents, checked Oct 23, 2026." schema={schema} crumbs={[['Home', '/'], ['Chatwoot pricing', '/pricing/chatwoot/']]}>
<div class="wrap page-head prose">
  <span class="eyebrow">Pricing guide · Checked on {CHECKED}</span>
  <h1>Chatwoot pricing: cloud plans vs self-hosting</h1>
  <p class="muted">I read the prices below off Chatwoot’s <a href={S.cloud}>cloud pricing page</a> and its <a href={S.self}>self-hosted plans page</a> on {CHECKED}, and the server needs off its <a href={S.req}>system requirements doc</a>. Everything is linked so you can check me. Prices change, so look at the source before you pay.</p>
  <p class="note"><b>Disclosure:</b> the “{aff.label}” link on this page is an affiliate link. If you buy a Chatwoot Cloud plan through it, we may earn {aff.terms}, at no extra cost to you. Self-hosting earns us nothing, and for a lot of teams it’s the cheaper pick. <a href="/disclosure/">How we make money</a>.</p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Two agents, light volume:</b> the free Hacker plan covers 2 agents and 500 conversations a month, live chat only.</li>
    <li><b>Paid cloud:</b> <b>$19 per agent/mo</b> (Startups) or <b>$39 per agent/mo</b> (Business, the one with automation rules).</li>
    <li><b>Self-hosted:</b> the Community Edition is <b>$0</b>. Budget about <b>$20–24/mo</b> for a 4 GB server, plus your time.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Chatwoot prices per agent, so the gap grows with every seat. The server cost doesn’t, at least until you’re handling thousands of conversations a day.</p>
</div>

<section style="padding-top:6px"><div class="wrap">
<h2>Chatwoot Cloud plans</h2>
<div class="compare-wrap"><table class="compare">
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Plan</th><th scope="col">Price</th><th scope="col">What you get (from Chatwoot’s page)</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>{cloud.map(p => <tr><th scope="row">{p.plan}</th><td><b class="usd">{p.price}</b></td><td>{p.note}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
</table></div>
<p class="note">Source: <a href={S.cloud}>chatwoot.com/pricing</a>, checked {CHECKED}. Every paid plan has a 15-day free trial. Extra Captain AI credits are $20 per 1,000. The page doesn’t say whether the per-agent prices assume monthly or yearly billing, so I haven’t guessed at a discount. Cloud data is hosted on AWS in the US, per Chatwoot’s FAQ.</p>
<p><a class="btn ghost" href={aff.href} rel="sponsored nofollow" data-track="outbound" data-tool={cw.slug} data-kind="affiliate">{aff.label} (affiliate link)</a></p>
</div></section>

<section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap">
<h2>Self-hosted plans</h2>
<div class="compare-wrap"><table class="compare">
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Plan</th><th scope="col">Price</th><th scope="col">What you get</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>{self.map(p => <tr><th scope="row">{p.plan}</th><td><b class="usd">{p.price}</b></td><td>{p.note}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
</table></div>
<p class="note">Source: <a href={S.self}>Chatwoot self-hosted plans</a>, checked {CHECKED}. One thing doesn’t line up on that page: the plan table marks Captain AI as Enterprise-only, but the FAQ says Premium Support includes it. Ask Chatwoot before buying Premium Support for the AI. Self-hosted Captain AI calls OpenAI’s models.</p>
</div></section>

<section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap">
<h2>What a team pays per month</h2>
<p class="muted">Agents × per-agent price. The self-hosted line is a flat ${SERVER}/mo DigitalOcean 4 GiB Droplet with no paid plan on top. Backups and your time are not in it.</p>
<figure class="chart" style="margin:0">
<svg viewBox="0 0 640 250" width="100%" role="img" aria-labelledby="cwchart-t">
  <title id="cwchart-t">Monthly cost of Chatwoot Startups, Business and self-hosted Community Edition for 2, 3, 5, 10 and 20 agents</title>
  {sizes.map((n, i) => {
    const y = 10 + i * 48; const wS = (n * 19 / maxV) * 420; const wB = (n * 39 / maxV) * 420; const wH = (SERVER / maxV) * 420;
    return <g>
      <text x="0" y={y + 12} font-size="13" fill="currentColor">{n} agents</text>
      <rect x="80" y={y} width={wS} height="12" fill="#8a8f98" />
      <text x={86 + wS} y={y + 10} font-size="11" fill="currentColor">${n * 19} Startups</text>
      <rect x="80" y={y + 14} width={wB} height="12" fill="#2f3a4a" />
      <text x={86 + wB} y={y + 24} font-size="11" fill="currentColor">${n * 39} Business</text>
      <rect x="80" y={y + 28} width={wH} height="12" fill="#c2410c" />
      <text x={86 + wH} y={y + 38} font-size="11" fill="currentColor">${SERVER} self-hosted</text>
    </g>;
  })}
</svg>
<figcaption class="note">Grey: Startups at $19/agent. Dark: Business at $39/agent. Red: one 4 GiB server at ${SERVER}/mo. Prices from <a href={S.cloud}>Chatwoot</a> on {CHECKED} and <a href={S.do}>DigitalOcean</a> on Oct 21, 2026.</figcaption>
</figure>
</div></section>

<section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap prose">
<h2>What self-hosting really takes</h2>
<p>From Chatwoot’s <a href={S.req}>system requirements</a>:</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>4 GB RAM</b> is the stated minimum, good for up to 10,000 conversations a day. Add at least 1 GB of swap so upgrades don’t run out of memory.</li>
  <li><b>CPU:</b> the docs recommend 4 cores for that same 10,000-a-day load. The pricing page FAQ says to start with 2. For a small team I think 2 vCPU is fine; that’s my judgment, not a load test.</li>
  <li><b>Postgres and Redis</b> are required. Postgres wants 5–10 GB of disk to start. S3-compatible storage is optional for attachments.</li>
  <li>Ubuntu is the only officially supported OS. The Sidekiq worker can grow past 1 GB of memory on a busy server.</li>
</ul>
<div class="compare-wrap"><table class="compare">
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Host</th><th scope="col">Plan</th><th scope="col">Spec</th><th scope="col">Price</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><th scope="row"><a href={S.vultr} rel="nofollow">Vultr</a></th><td>Cloud Compute, Regular</td><td>2 vCPU · 4 GB · 80 GB SSD</td><td>$20.00/mo</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row"><a href={S.do} rel="nofollow">DigitalOcean</a></th><td>Basic Droplet</td><td>2 vCPU · 4 GiB · 80 GiB SSD</td><td>$24.00/mo</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p class="note">Prices read from Vultr and DigitalOcean on Oct 21, 2026. Backups cost extra (DigitalOcean 20% weekly or 30% daily; Vultr 20%). For email notifications and an email inbox channel you’ll also need an SMTP service.</p>

<h2>So which should you pick?</h2>
<ul>
  <li><b>One or two people, a website chat widget:</b> the free Hacker plan. Watch the 500-conversation cap and the 30-day retention.</li>
  <li><b>3+ agents and nobody wants to run a server:</b> Startups at $19/agent, or Business at $39 if you need automation rules. Five agents on Business is $195 a month, so do the sum before you pick it.</li>
  <li><b>3+ agents and someone is comfortable with Docker:</b> self-host the Community Edition. At 5 agents it’s ~$24 against $95–195 a month on the cloud. You give up Captain AI and voice, and you own upgrades and backups.</li>
  <li><b>Need SSO or an SLA on your own servers:</b> Enterprise Edition at $99/agent. At that price, compare it with the cloud Enterprise quote too.</li>
</ul>

<h2>FAQ</h2>
{faq.map(f => <><h3>{f.q}</h3><p>{f.a}</p></>)}
</div></section>

<section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap">
<div class="sec-head"><h2>Chatwoot on SelfHost Office</h2></div>
<p><a class="tool" href={`/tool/${cw.slug}/`}><img src={avatar(cw, 56)} alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"/> Chatwoot</a>: {cw.stars.toLocaleString('en-US')} GitHub stars, last push {fmtDate(cw.lastPush)} (GitHub API, fetched {fmtDate(cw.fetchedAt)}).</p>
</div></section>
</Base>
